From 6a6eeb8fc4a7e8b294068c56b977cc22dc2b6e46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joonhoekim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 01:28:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/56] usb: gadget: f_ncm: restart the TX timer when the
 freelist is empty

The same fix as upstream's "usb: gadget:
f_ncm: restart the TX timer if the TX freelist is empty" (Cosmin Tanislav,
2026-08, Fixes: 6d3865f9d41f) / "Restart timer when eth_start_xmit()
fails" (Francesco Lavra, 2026-07), which this tree predates.

When the 300 us flush timer fires while no USB request is free,
eth_start_xmit(NULL) returns NETDEV_TX_BUSY and the timer does not run
again until a new NTB is started: the half-filled NTB (ping replies, TCP
ACKs) sits until more traffic fills it. On TB323FU the USB network stopped
now and then (link UP, ARP REACHABLE, no replies) until the gadget was
rebound. Re-arm the timer instead.
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
index 500c9c19c..04d7372d5 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
@@ -1158,7 +1158,15 @@ static enum hrtimer_restart ncm_tx_timeout(struct hrtimer *data)
 		 *
 		 * This will call directly into u_ether's eth_start_xmit()
 		 */
-		netdev->netdev_ops->ndo_start_xmit(NULL, netdev);
+		if (netdev->netdev_ops->ndo_start_xmit(NULL, netdev) == NETDEV_TX_BUSY) {
+			/*
+			 * No free request to send the pending NTB: try again
+			 * later, or it waits for the next datagram, which may
+			 * never come (the link stalls).
+			 */
+			hrtimer_forward_now(data, TX_TIMEOUT_NSECS);
+			return HRTIMER_RESTART;
+		}
 	}
 	return HRTIMER_NORESTART;
 }
